WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Test 3. This is the IELTS listening test.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
and you will have a chance to check your work.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
All the recordings will be played once only.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The test is in four parts.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
At the end of the test you will be given 10 minutes

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
to transfer your answers to the answer sheet.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Now turn to part 1.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.000
You will hear a woman phoning to ask about a summer cycling camp

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.000
for her young son who is called Charlie.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
First you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Hello. Junior Cycle Camp. Jake speaking.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Hi. I'm calling for some information about the cycle camp.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
I'm thinking of sending my son.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Great. Well, it's held every weekday morning over the summer vacation

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.000
and we focus on basic cycling skills and safety.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.000
We have 8 levels for children from 3 years upwards.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
How old's your son?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Charlie? He's 7. He can ride a bike,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000
but he needs a little more training before he's safe to go on the road.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.000
He'd probably be best in level 5.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.000
They start off practicing on the site here,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
and we aim to get them riding on the road,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
but first they're taken to ride in the park, away from the traffic.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Right. And can you tell me a bit about the instructors?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Well, all our staff wear different colored shirts.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.000
So we have 3 supervisors and they have red shirts.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
They support the instructors and they also stand in for me if I'm not around.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Then the instructors themselves are in blue shirts,

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.000
and one of these is responsible for each class.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Okay.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.000
In order to be accepted,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
all our instructors have to submit a reference

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
from someone who's seen them work with children,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:17.000
like if they've worked as a babysitter, for example.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Then they have to complete our training course,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000
including how to do lesson plans,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.000
and generally care for the well-being of the kids in their class.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.000
They do a great job, I have to say.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Right. And tell me a bit about the classes.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
What size will Charlie's class be?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.000
We have a limit of 8 children in each class.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.000
So their instructor really gets to know them well.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
They're out riding most of the time,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
but they have quiet times too,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.000
where their instructor might tell them a story

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.000
that's got something to do with cycling,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.000
or get them to play a game together.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
It's a lot of fun.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
It must be.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.000
Now, what happens if there's rain?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.000
Do the classes still run?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Oh yes. We don't let that put us off.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.000
We just put on our waterproofs and keep cycling.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.000
Before you hear the rest of the conversation,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.000
you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:58.000
And is there anything special Charlie should bring along with him?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Well, maybe some spare clothes,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.000
or a pair of shoes,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.000
or a pair of shoes,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.000
or a pair of shoes,

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.000
Well, maybe some spare clothes,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.000
especially if the weather's not so good.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.000
And a snack for break time?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.000
How about a drink?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.000
No, we'll provide that.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.000
And make sure he has shoes, not sandals.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Sure.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.000
And just at present,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.000
Charlie has to take medication every few hours,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.000
so I'll make sure he has that.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Absolutely.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.000
Just give us details of when he has to take it,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.000
and we'll make sure he does.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Thanks.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:59.000
Now, there are a few things you should know about Day 1 of the camp.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.000
The classes normally start at 9.30 every morning.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:10.000
But on Day 1, you should aim to get Charlie here by 9.20.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:16.000
The finishing time will be 12.30, as usual.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.000
We need the additional time because there are a few extra things to do.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.000
The most important is that we have a very careful check

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:32.000
to make sure that every child's helmet fits properly.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:39.000
If it doesn't fit, we'll try to adjust it, or we'll find him another one.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.000
But he must wear it all the time he's on the bike.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Of course.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:51.000
Then, after that, all the instructors will be waiting to meet their classes,

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
and they'll meet up in the tent.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
You can't miss it.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:02.000
And each instructor will take their class away and get started.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.000
Okay, well, that all sounds good.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Now, can you tell me how much the camp costs a week?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.000
$199.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:22.000
We've managed to keep the price more or less the same as last year.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.000
It was $190 then.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.000
But the places are filling up quite quickly.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Right. Okay, well, I'd like to book for the...

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.000
I'd like to book for the...

